From 9d917db68fe6ad38b1718902389d234a8c6422e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:14:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 121/210] media: amlogic: amvdec: add H.264 decoding

Decode frame-based H.264 slice requests with multi-instance firmware.
Validate SPS/PPS and slice syntax, synthesize in-band headers and build
frame and field reference lists from request controls and timestamps.

Keep parser scratch in the session and retain the direct-input buffer
until decode completion. Track field-pair provenance and canvas lifetime,
program colocated motion-vector storage and stop processor DMA before
releasing request buffers. Advertise profiles and levels from the
per-compatible capability tables.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5 Claude:claude-fable-5.1 Codex:gpt-5.6 Codex:gpt-6.0
[chewitt: state the H.264 capabilities in each per-SoC format table
 instead of a shared GX macro, and allow 32 CAPTURE buffers, the size
 of the firmware canvas table; a level 5.1 stream decoded by a client
 with six frame threads needs more than 24; allocate each colocated
 MV slot when its canvas is first decoded into rather than all 32 at
 stream start, which saves ~50 MB of CMA on a 4K stream]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
